P-I7, spec 001 group 6 (W1; tasks.md T073, T164): the shared state's protected parts, for the Author's hand.

Group 6 had no protected file before W1's regrouping; the shared state on the tunnel end gives it three (tasks.md,
Format, "Patches"). It applies after P-I3, whose iam.tf, bridge, and contract rows it changes: each hunk is against the
text P-I3 leaves.
  - infra/prod/iam.tf: the tunnel end's role reads the shared state's parameters, its own path as before, and the two
    role passwords of /h4reet/ec2/ its roles target sets, by name (DB_GATEWAY_PASSWORD, DB_GRAFANA_RO_PASSWORD), and
    may put the hourly backup under the backups' bucket's dumps/ prefix, and nothing that reads, lists, or deletes
    there (contracts/shared-state.md §1, §2, §8);
  - infra/lambdas/alert_bridge/bridge.py: shared_state_backup_failed, the tunnel end's backup timer's kind, with its
    page, docs/runbooks/shared-state.md; test_bridge.py its notice;
  - specs/001-cloud-elevation/contracts/aws-alerts.md §2: its row, which the bridge's own test holds to a notice, so the
    row travels with the bridge that knows it, as P-I3's did.
infra/test/test_prod_network.py and test_prod_shared_state.py read iam.tf as P-I3 and then P-I7 leave it
(infra/test/patches.py). On an export with P-I3 and P-I7: the bridge's tests and the prod root's checks pass.

Built from plain copies (the text P-I3 leaves, into $TMPDIR), edited, then diff -u with a/ and b/ labels; never git
apply. Apply it on W1's -p branch after P-I3, with `patch -p1 < <this file>` at the repository's root.
